# Line endings.
#
# This repository is edited on Windows and every script in it runs on Linux,
# inside a container. Git stores LF, but a checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites the working tree to CRLF — and `docker build` copies the working
# tree, not the commit. A shell script that arrives with CRLF has a shebang of
# `#!/bin/sh\r`, so the kernel looks for an interpreter with a carriage return
# in its name, and the container dies with:
#
#   exec /usr/local/bin/migrate-entrypoint.sh failed: No such file or directory
#
# which is exit 127 and reads like a missing file rather than a missing
# newline. CI never sees it either: a Linux runner checks out LF whatever this
# setting says, so the build passes there and fails on the machine that deploys.
#
# Normalising everything to LF removes the whole class of problem. There are no
# Windows batch or PowerShell scripts in this repository; add an `eol=crlf`
# line here if one is ever added.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so Git never tries to "fix" the bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.gz binary
